WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:06.257
In Eastern Spain, in the City of Valls, there's&nbsp;
a legendary onion.

00:00:06.257 --> 00:00:10.014
Locals will tell you that at the end of the 19th century,

00:00:10.014 --> 00:00:13.680
a farmer named&nbsp;
Xat De Benaiges carried out an experiment...

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.740
He planted a crop of onions but&nbsp;
instead of letting them grow as&nbsp;usual,

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.345
he increased the depth of the&nbsp;
soil above them as they grew.&nbsp;

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.201
...this caused the stems to lengthen and remain white.

00:00:28.201 --> 00:00:32.706
Not as sharp as a spring onion and not as subtle as a leak,

00:00:32.706 --> 00:00:40.587
these onions, called "calçots", are mild,&nbsp;
sweet and most importantly, exceptionally delicious.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:51.780
Not long after the onion's creation, local&nbsp;
families began hosting calçot eating&nbsp;parties

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:58.193
...and in 1982 the onion was granted its&nbsp;
own Festival: The Gran festa de la Calçotada. 

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.280
The Calçots are cooked over hot coals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:25.614
and grapevine clippings giving them a&nbsp;
rich smoky flavor.

00:01:27.068 --> 00:01:33.532
The burnt outer layer is removed and the inner part is dipped in a tomato and garlic salbitxada (salbichada) sauce.

00:01:49.335 --> 00:01:53.365
Local farmers participate in a competition for the best calçot.&nbsp;

00:01:54.511 --> 00:01:55.615
This is Dalmaci. 

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:59.174
He’s a seasoned calçot grower and an esteemed competition judge.

00:02:41.882 --> 00:02:47.176
While the onions are the main event, there's&nbsp;
plenty more to do including a grand parade...

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:54.120
a competition for the best sauce and a&nbsp;
selection of meats and sausages to try... 

00:02:55.260 --> 00:03:00.960
So no one gets thirsty, local wine is readily&nbsp;
available, served from a traditional porrón. 

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.987
But, when it comes to eating calçots,

00:03:06.987 --> 00:03:10.866
some festival-goers have a little more experience than others...

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.560
This year, Adria ate 221 calçots!

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:26.411
That's&nbsp;more than 3 kilos in just 45 minutes

00:04:16.291 --> 00:04:18.766
In a world full of onions that will make you cry,

00:04:18.766 --> 00:04:24.236
the smile you get from a calçot is something worth celebrating…

